cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the populism axis measure, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "populism-axis: a training-free measure of populist rhetoric"
abstract: >-
  Python and R software for the populism axis, a training-free measure of populist
  rhetoric built from written anchor propositions in a pretrained sentence-embedding
  space, with an entailment-based claim check. Also defines continuous text scales
  from user-written propositions.
authors:
  - family-names: "Tomašević"
    given-names: "Aleksandar"
    email: "atomashevic@gmail.com"
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/atomashevic/populism-axis"
keywords:
  - populism
  - political communication
  - text as data
  - sentence embeddings
  - natural language inference
